WEBVTT

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:06.150
City is united as one! We're all friends!

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:09.120
Sounding great, everyone!

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:14.850
Okay, what's the first match of 
the Friendship Cup's second day?

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:18.600
It's Yuya Sakaki versus Duel Chaser 227.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:21.570
What kind of fight will they have for us?

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:23.040
Yuya!

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:31.690
Yuya...

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:36.890
Hey! I'm the one who'd give Yuya 
the most exciting fight!

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:38.250
They're so clueless...

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:49.630
I'll escort you to the venue.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:57.370
The card you gave me...

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:02.040
You said you wanted me to win 
and return it to Jack, right?

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:07.370
But for me to win means

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:10.900
someone else will get sent underground.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.970
Before I win... No, before I duel...

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:17.800
There's something I have to do!

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.560
D-Wheels.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.800
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.420
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:30.880
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:33.080
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:11.340
The Silver Sword

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:19.010
First, Duel Chaser 227 enters the arena!

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:22.280
He lost a duel during a car chase,

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:25.980
and was cast out of the Duel Chasers. 
Quite an unlucky fellow!

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:29.050
Today, he'll be competing as a Commons!

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:31.790
Wow, unlucky for him.

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:35.760
But he's enrolled under his Duel Chasers title.

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:45.440
Can you return to the Duel Chasers 
with your honor intact?

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:48.410
All of that rides on this duel.

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:51.380
Now, Yuya Sakaki enters!

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:02.250
Hey, now... Why are you booing?

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:08.930
Look! This happened because 
you wouldn't send me in.

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:13.350
Yuya... My feelings reached you, right?

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:25.340
Okay, everyone! Let's get excited!

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:27.130
Action Field...

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:28.230
Wait!

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:32.150
Everyone, this is the Friendship Cup.

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:35.820
Do you know what happens to 
the losers of these duels?

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:39.290
They're sent to an underground 
waste-processing facility!

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:43.900
Underground?

00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:47.870
Those sent underground never get out again.

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:50.840
They're made to do hard labor for life!

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:52.550
Oh, no.

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:55.690
Then, Mr. Tokumatsu, who lost to me...

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:57.310
And Gongenzaka, as well?

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:02.010
Tsukikage, too...

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:05.240
Oh, that's all it was?

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:08.590
Your friends don't seem to understand

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:11.120
how a competitive society works.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:15.460
At this rate, I wonder if we 
can even fight together.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:24.830
Fool.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:29.720
What's wrong with that, exactly?

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:34.180
It's natural for losers to end 
up at the bottom, isn't it?

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:36.150
Yeah!

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:38.350
Natural?! How can you...

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:41.340
Yuya, winning is the most important thing.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.090
Action Field, on.

00:05:43.430 --> 00:05:46.060
Field Spell Crossover Acceleration.

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:50.730
Wait! I'm not finished talking—

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:55.000
Duel Mode, on. Autopilot, stand by.

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:03.480
Riding duel...

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:05.780
Acceleration!

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:07.430
Duel!

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:17.320
Around the first corner... And the first 
turn goes to Duel Chaser 227!

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:22.030
Sending losing duelists to do hard 
labor underground is wrong!

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:25.770
He's just worried about losing his first time!

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:29.570
After being crushed by Jack 
like that, it makes sense!

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:33.970
Fighting duels that make other 
people miserable is wrong!

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:39.770
People only listen to the thoughts 
and opinions of winners.

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:43.980
To cry about that, without even fighting...

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:47.210
That is why I accuse you of self-satisfaction.

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:50.410
Duels exist to make everyone smile!

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:51.750
Enough!

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:55.640
Did you come here to make speeches?

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:57.230
Then we don't need you here.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.330
Just surrender and get out!

00:07:02.390 --> 00:07:03.440
My turn.

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:05.540
I summon Jutte Lord from my hand!

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:12.190
When I successfully summon Jutte Lord,

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:16.180
I can Special Summon another 
Jutte monster from my hand.

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:18.090
Come out, Jutte Fighter!

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:24.490
Level 2 Jutte Lord tunes Level 4 Jutte Fighter!

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:30.550
Come out, hunter with the authority of law!

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:33.260
Synchro Summon!

00:07:33.770 --> 00:07:36.090
Level 6 Goyo Predator!

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:41.910
And from my hand, I activate 
Equip Spell Goyo Arrow!

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:47.080
This card can only be equipped to Goyo monsters.

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:49.770
I equip it to Goyo Predator!

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:53.020
I activate Goyo Arrow's effect!

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:57.980
Once per turn, the equipped monster 
can deal damage to you,

00:07:57.980 --> 00:07:59.670
equal to its level times 100.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:02.110
Goyo Predator is Level 6.

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:03.870
Therefore, it deals you 600 damage!

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.700
I end my turn.

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:11.600
This is incredible...

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:15.470
Even though he couldn't attack on the first turn,

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:17.940
Duel Chaser 227 still dealt Yuya damage!

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:20.140
Now, it's your turn.

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:23.960
What will you do? Going to fight a 
duel in this "wrong" tournament?

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:27.740
If you won't listen when I talk...

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:30.620
My turn! Draw!

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:37.600
I set the Pendulum Scale with Scale 3 
Performapal Odd-Eyes Light Phoenix

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:42.660
and Scale 8 Performapal Odd-Eyes Unicorn!

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:55.580
Now I can summon monsters between 
Levels 4 and 7 simultaneously!

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:00.020
Swing, my soul's pendulum!

00:09:00.550 --> 00:09:02.990
Draw an arc of light in the sky!

00:09:02.990 --> 00:09:04.500
Pendulum Summon!

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:07.690
Come out, my monsters!

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:12.230
First, Performapal Bot-Eyes Lizard!

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:15.160
And then, Performapal Fireflux!

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:18.440
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:24.180
I'm about to show you some surprising illusions 
that will bring smiles to your faces!

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:26.040
Battle.

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:29.410
I attack Goyo Predator with Bot-Eyes Lizard!

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:35.440
Attacking 2400-attack-point Goyo Predator 
with a 1600-attack-point monster?

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:36.890
How reckless!

00:09:37.460 --> 00:09:41.090
I activate Performapal Odd-Eyes 
Unicorn's Pendulum Effect!

00:09:41.420 --> 00:09:47.570
Once per turn, I can add its attack points to 
those of one Odd-Eyes monster in battle.

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:51.770
What did he say? An Odd-Eyes isn't fighting!

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:56.980
Now, please keep your eyes on Bot-Eyes Lizard.

00:09:57.290 --> 00:10:01.080
I can declare the name of an Odd-Eyes monster,

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:03.720
and Bot-Eyes will be treated as that monster.

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:05.920
And the name that I declare is...

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:07.930
Odd-Eyes Dragon!

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:15.480
I add Performapal Fireflux's 1200 
attack points to its own!

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:26.300
He destroyed Goyo Predator, along with 
the Goyo Arrow equipped to it!

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:29.770
Now, I attack directly with Fireflux!

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:37.550
Yuya took damage first,

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:40.420
but he's turned it around in a flash!

00:10:40.730 --> 00:10:42.720
When the Battle Phase ends,

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:46.160
Odd-Eyes Unicorn's Pendulum 
Effect ends, as well.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:49.130
I now end my turn.

00:10:49.130 --> 00:10:51.370
He's better than I thought.

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:54.100
Because he isn't fighting Jack, of course.

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:57.750
I'll win... I'll win and return to the Tops.

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:00.070
I'll become a Duel Chaser again!

00:11:00.770 --> 00:11:01.810
My turn!

00:11:02.170 --> 00:11:04.810
I activate my spell card Monster Reborn!

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:07.910
Return to me, Goyo Predator!

00:11:09.010 --> 00:11:14.250
Wow! The just-defeated Predator 
is immediately reborn!

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:18.090
I attack Bot-Eyes Lizard with Goyo Predator!

00:11:23.430 --> 00:11:26.360
Yuya's moving to take an Action Card!

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:30.030
I don't think so!

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:37.710
Yuya!

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:43.690
Duel Chaser 227 blocked Yuya 
from the Action Card.

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:45.380
Kind of rough play, but not bad!

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:53.520
I activate Goyo Predator's effect.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:56.110
When it destroys a monster by battle,

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:58.300
I can Special Summon that monster 
to my side of the field!

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:01.500
Come to me, Bot-Eyes Lizard!

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:07.910
Duel Chaser 227 took Yuya's monster for himself!

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:11.610
I attack Fireflux with Bot-Eyes Lizard!

00:12:16.280 --> 00:12:18.020
I end my turn.

00:12:18.410 --> 00:12:23.490
Duel Chaser 227's series of attacks 
have dealt more damage to Yuya!

00:12:23.490 --> 00:12:26.550
It isn't over yet... The fun is only getting started!

00:12:26.950 --> 00:12:27.930
My turn!

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:34.580
I Pendulum Summon with the 
Pendulum Scale already set!

00:12:37.070 --> 00:12:40.300
Return from my Extra Deck, Performapal Fireflux!

00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:44.910
And from my hand, the rare dragon 
with two different-colored eyes...

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:47.830
Come out, Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:12:51.260 --> 00:12:57.040
If he attacks Level 5 Goyo Predator now, 
he can use Odd-Eyes Unicorn's effect

00:12:57.040 --> 00:13:01.930
to add Fireflux's attack points to Odd-Eyes 
Pendulum Dragon's, which can use

00:13:01.930 --> 00:13:04.400
its own effect to double the damage.

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:11.770
Yuya will win for sure.

00:13:13.470 --> 00:13:16.440
Can Yuya finish it with this battle?

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:18.200
Do it! Do it!

00:13:18.200 --> 00:13:19.910
Get him!

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:31.520
Do it! Do it! Do it!

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:32.800
Finish him off!

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:34.990
No mercy!

00:13:34.990 --> 00:13:44.440
Do it! Do it! Do it!

00:13:44.730 --> 00:13:47.410
If I attack now, I'll win.

00:13:47.410 --> 00:13:50.110
But then he'll be sent underground...

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:54.440
There!

00:14:05.290 --> 00:14:08.600
Duel Chaser 227 got the Action Card!

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:10.760
Magnificent D-Wheel control!

00:14:11.350 --> 00:14:14.420
I activate my Action Card Battle Lock!

00:14:14.420 --> 00:14:18.240
This turn, you cannot declare battle!

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:23.540
Your fun ends here.

00:14:24.520 --> 00:14:27.350
He missed his chance to win...

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:31.020
What are you doing?!

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:32.700
Don't you want to win?

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:34.380
This is boring!

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:35.990
I end my turn.

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:43.560
A duelist who hesitates cannot seize 
the hearts of the spectators.

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:45.050
Yuya...

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:48.840
It seems the goddess of fortune is on my side.

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:50.500
My turn!

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:56.730
I summon Stygian Security from my hand.

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:03.930
Level 1 Stygian Security tunes 
Level 4 Bot-Eyes Lizard!

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:08.550
Pursue him to the ends of hell!

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:11.390
Appear, sacred soul!

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:13.590
Synchro Summon!

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:17.460
Come out, Level 5 Goyo Chaser!

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:21.240
Director!

00:15:21.240 --> 00:15:26.040
With this card you gave me, 
I shall bring you victory!

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:28.740
I activate my spell card Polymerization!

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:30.710
Polymerization?

00:15:30.710 --> 00:15:35.360
The soul of the unwavering pursuer 
and the soul of the proud predator

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:37.680
become one and transcend!

00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:39.380
Fusion Summon!

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:43.740
Come out, heir to the noble predator's soul,

00:15:43.740 --> 00:15:45.130
Goyo Emperor!

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:48.730
What a shock...

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:52.800
Duel Chaser 227 performed a Fusion Summon!

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:57.240
Fusion?

00:15:58.070 --> 00:16:02.330
Does that mean a rat has infiltrated this dimension?

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:04.240
Let's go.

00:16:04.240 --> 00:16:08.120
I attack Odd-Eyes Pendulum 
Dragon with Goyo Emperor!

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:16.720
Yuya's monster was destroyed!

00:16:17.510 --> 00:16:19.690
I activate Goyo Emperor's effect.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:24.600
I negate the destruction of one of 
your cards destroyed in battle!

00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:28.370
Huh? He didn't destroy it?

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:32.590
However, I gain control of 
the monster I destroyed.

00:16:36.240 --> 00:16:38.330
As long as I have Goyo Emperor,

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:41.980
I can take control of all your ace monsters.

00:16:43.710 --> 00:16:47.460
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon, attack Fireflux!

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:58.200
When Goyo Emperor captures
 Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon,

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:00.800
it can use Goyo Emperor's effect!

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:04.970
I negate the monster's destruction 
and assume control of it!

00:17:08.340 --> 00:17:11.740
Yuya's lost control of two monsters!

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:13.900
A direct attack will finish this.

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:15.280
It's over!

00:17:15.280 --> 00:17:16.980
Finish him!

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:21.800
This is checkmate!

00:17:23.440 --> 00:17:27.160
What are you doing, Yuya? The crowd's 
turning against you!

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:28.620
Yuya?

00:17:29.420 --> 00:17:33.830
Let's send this loser to a pathetic defeat!

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:44.180
Go! I attack directly with Fireflux!

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:51.620
I activate the Pendulum Effect 
of Odd-Eyes Light Phoenix!

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:53.580
When I'm attacked directly,

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:57.140
it can destroy one card in my Pendulum 
Zone other than itself,

00:17:57.970 --> 00:17:59.920
to let me Special Summon it!

00:17:59.920 --> 00:18:03.990
Yuya summoned a monster 
with 2000 attack points!

00:18:04.240 --> 00:18:08.980
Duel Chaser 227 can't attack directly 
or destroy Light Phoenix!

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:10.370
Pointless struggles.

00:18:10.760 --> 00:18:11.740
I end my turn!

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:14.710
Yuya's barely managed to hang in there!

00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:18.180
But he's taken huge damage! 
Can he turn it back around?

00:18:24.850 --> 00:18:26.900
My turn!

00:18:32.480 --> 00:18:36.180
I activate my spell card Double Reborn Level 4!

00:18:36.860 --> 00:18:42.130
We can each Special Summon one Level 4 monster 
from the graveyard, in defense position.

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:43.710
What? Me, too?

00:18:43.710 --> 00:18:44.770
Now, summon!

00:18:45.570 --> 00:18:47.580
I don't know your angle, but...

00:18:47.580 --> 00:18:49.240
Come out, Jutte Lord!

00:18:51.710 --> 00:18:55.430
Be reborn, Performapal Bot-Eyes Lizard!

00:18:57.350 --> 00:19:02.010
Bot-Eyes's effect lets me treat 
it as Odd-Eyes Dragon!

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:08.910
And by tributing one Light Attribute Monster 
on my side of the field, Light Phoenix,

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:11.100
I can make Odd-Eyes Dragon evolve!

00:19:11.590 --> 00:19:12.800
Evolve?

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:21.910
Come out! Light of salvation that shines 
through the darkness of despair!

00:19:24.480 --> 00:19:26.840
Odd-Eyes Saber Dragon!

00:19:30.050 --> 00:19:34.520
Battle! I attack Jutte Lord with 
Odd-Eyes Saber Dragon!

00:19:40.350 --> 00:19:42.480
But I take no damage!

00:19:42.480 --> 00:19:43.930
I'm just getting started.

00:19:43.930 --> 00:19:46.530
I activate Odd-Eyes Saber Dragon's effect!

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:51.100
When this card destroys a monster by 
battle, sending it to the graveyard,

00:19:51.100 --> 00:19:53.290
I destroy another of your monsters.

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:54.000
What?

00:19:54.440 --> 00:19:56.420
I destroy Goyo Emperor!

00:19:58.250 --> 00:20:01.610
When Goyo Emperor is destroyed, its effect ends!

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:04.300
I regain control of my monsters!

00:20:06.240 --> 00:20:09.320
Yuya took back his stolen monsters!

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:11.800
Looking great! Push him back more!

00:20:11.800 --> 00:20:13.790
Now it's getting interesting!

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:18.310
I attack directly with Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:21.040
Damn it!

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:33.150
I will be the one...

00:20:33.150 --> 00:20:34.310
...to win!

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:37.530
I got it.

00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:39.480
Action Card Evade!

00:20:39.820 --> 00:20:42.060
Action Card No Action!

00:20:42.060 --> 00:20:45.460
I negate an Action Spell's activation 
and effect, destroying it!

00:21:06.390 --> 00:21:07.370
Yuya...

00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:12.520
Was that what you wanted to get across?

00:21:15.220 --> 00:21:18.460
Oh? So that is his true nature...

00:21:18.810 --> 00:21:23.430
Then 227's loss was not for nothing, after all.

00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:29.900
Yuya, well done.

00:21:30.220 --> 00:21:33.370
You let your chance for victory 
slip away into certain doom,

00:21:33.370 --> 00:21:34.760
then bounced right back.

00:21:34.760 --> 00:21:36.110
You gave us quite a show!

00:21:36.110 --> 00:21:38.440
Looking good! That was great!

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:39.580
Amazing!

00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:42.620
Yuya! Yuya! Yuya!

00:21:42.620 --> 00:21:45.830
No... This isn't right.

00:21:45.830 --> 00:21:48.050
This isn't the type of duel I believe in!

00:21:54.400 --> 00:21:57.460
Stop... Stop!

00:21:57.790 --> 00:21:58.780
Don't do this!

00:21:58.780 --> 00:22:00.730
Don't take him underground!

00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:05.190
Get away.

00:22:05.830 --> 00:22:06.840
Let me go!

00:22:07.130 --> 00:22:09.670
Please, let me go!

00:23:47.060 --> 00:23:48.540
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:23:48.540 --> 00:23:52.540
The Friendship Cup's star, 
Shingo Sawatari, is here!

00:23:52.860 --> 00:23:55.960
The crowd is going wild. Everyone is cheering.

00:23:55.960 --> 00:23:59.020
This is a stage made for me alone.

00:23:59.020 --> 00:24:02.790
Yeah, yeah, yeah! I'm finally here!

00:24:02.790 --> 00:24:08.230
Watch me, Rin... I'll win and 
see my promise through!

00:24:08.230 --> 00:24:13.200
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
Dragon Slaying!! Hugo Versus Sawatari.

00:24:13.200 --> 00:24:15.210
The fun is only getting started!
